"edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/step5-opus-aa-1017-omp36-aa/omp-36/cells/aa-2/trig-omp-reported/18/workspace", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "aa-2", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/17.3.8 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cache/bin/omp/5347ff91e8f44f2c69a79d7b152b7301687cd5c8/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py`, and all 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass.\n\n**Cause:** `strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")` only matches timestamps with no timezone, so the trailing `Z` in `\"2026-10-12T08:30:00Z\"` was left over and raised the error.\n\n**Fix:** `parse_date` now changes a trailing `Z` to `+00:00` and parses with `datetime.fromisoformat`. Python only accepts `Z` there from 3.11, so the swap makes it work on older versions too.\n\n**One behaviour change:** timestamps ending in `Z` or an offset now come back timezone-aware (UTC). Timestamps without one still come back naive, as before.\n\n- Comparing an aware datetime with a naive one, or subtracting one from the other, raises a `TypeError`. Any code that mixes the two from this feed will need to handle that.\n- `day_key` still returns the date exactly as written, with no timezone conversion.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 7, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 79758, "requests_cache_write": 103831, "reques